1
00:05:12,631 --> 00:05:18,631
Centuries ago one man was chosen to protect all that is good. But an enemy from
the past has traveled through time to challenge him in the present.

2
00:10:25,263 --> 00:10:31,263
Highlander III: The Sorcerer is a fantasy, action,
adventure film directed by Andrew Morahan.

3
00:15:37,894 --> 00:15:43,894
Starts off in the 15th century, with Connor McLeod training with
another immortal swordsman, the Japanese sorcerer Nakano.

4
00:20:50,526 --> 00:20:56,526
When an evil immortal named Kane kills the old wizard, the
resulting battle leaves him buried in an underground cave.

5
00:26:03,157 --> 00:26:09,157
When Kane resurfaces in the 20th century to create
havoc, it's up to McLeod to stop him.

6
00:31:15,789 --> 00:31:21,789
Connor 'The Highlander' MacLeod, played by Christopher Lambert.

7
00:36:28,421 --> 00:36:34,421
Kane, played by Mario Van Peebles.

8
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Alex Johnson / Sarah, played by Deborah Kara Unger.

9
00:46:53,684 --> 00:46:59,684
Nakano, played by Mako.

10
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:12,315
Lt. John Stenn, played by Martin Neufeld.

11
00:57:18,947 --> 00:57:24,947
Takamura, played by Daniel Dõ.

12
01:02:31,578 --> 01:02:37,578
Highlander III: The Sorcerer (also known as Highlander: The Final Dimension or Highlander: The Final Conflict) is a 1994
British-Canadian-French action-adventure fantasy film and the third installment in the Highlander film series.

13
01:07:44,210 --> 01:07:50,210
Set as an alternate sequel to the original film (i.e., it completely ignores and frequently contradicts the events of
Highlander II: The Quickening), it is the final Highlander film to focus on Connor MacLeod as the protagonist.

14
01:12:56,842 --> 01:13:02,842
In the film, Connor MacLeod is forced to face a new, dangerous enemy, a powerful sorcerer known as Kane who
threatens to win the fabled "Prize" in order to gain world domination by eliminating MacLeod.

15
01:18:09,473 --> 01:18:15,473
It grossed $36.7 million worldwide, becoming the highest grossing film in the
franchise, as well as the only one to recover its budget at the box office.

16
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
It received mostly negative reviews from critics, although it
was considered better than the previous film.

17
01:28:34,736 --> 01:28:40,736
The film explores themes of new york city, martial
arts, japan, magic, immortality.

18
01:33:47,368 --> 01:33:53,368
The tone is dark.
